  "rationale": "Retained specific comparison from active record b0aeec2edd679b68496db11c525f09dd3a4e92f161da06ad4a54e6686d87979e: Destructor extension author review. FunctionsDestructors.step_correspondence is an iff between any destructor-machine successor of an embedded Functions configuration and an embedded Functions Step successor, assuming ExitAllowed. ExitAllowed checks all possible result evaluations of exhausted bodies for StoreFinished and is vacuous for nonempty code. The maps preserve ordinary names, calls, local statements, signatures, stores and stack order. raw_backward and step_backward handle arbitrary successors, while collect proves GC commutation. The stated boundary explicitly excludes preservation of all old program typings/exits and does not claim an unconditional equivalence. Differential renewal: the sole changed required input is unit:shared.typing.realization, deleting the obsolete word \"five\" from \"The five structural clauses\". The linked shared.well_formed definition now lists six grouped structural clauses, represented by seven WellFormedWith fields because object-key and variable-key uniqueness share a prose bullet. Realizes.ownership still requires the complete WellFormedWith predicate with pending roots; the correction neither changes an assumption nor adds declaration-kind invariants to realization. Every other required raw unit, formal selection, and policy has identical path/content hash to the prior reviewed packet. New Assignment proofs do not alter this earlier-language claim.\nAssignment-notation renewal: every input to the preceding subject-specific comparison is byte-identical except context:AGENTS.md, whose sole edit replaces the documented concrete spelling `store p, e` with `p = e`. The abstract Statement.store constructor, typing, execution, and proofs are unchanged. This spelling change does not alter the preceding comparison or any audit classification and span for this subject.",
